e-cyber-law walkthrough log — 2026-10-10
Worked-case lesson: no command line by design (brief §6).
The "run" is the compliance-mapping matrix authored and self-reviewed
in-session against GDPR articles read directly from the EUR-Lex full text
(fetched 2026-10-10 via browser_open; curl was bot-walled).

Scope: fictional Bluefin Retail (US e-commerce, 180 staff, EU customers; names,
addresses, payment tokens, purchase history, loyalty analytics). Matrix rows
(7): Art 6/7 marketing consent -> affirmative opt-in w/ consent records;
Art 30 records of processing -> build versioned register; Art 33/34 breach
runbook rewrite (72h authority clock, processor clause, high-risk templates);
Art 35 DPIA for loyalty profiling before next retrain; Art 37/38 DPO
designation w/ CEO reporting line; Chapter V transfer basis per US-processing
flow; Art 83 two-tier fine exposure board brief. Every row: numbered
obligation, owner, control, evidence artifact, test cadence.
GDPR articles verified in-session: 5 (principles + accountability), 6 (lawful
bases), 7 (consent conditions), 33 (72h notification), 34 (data-subject
communication), 35 (DPIA), 37/38 (DPO designation + independence), 83 (fine
tiers 10M/2% and 20M/4%). EU AI Act (Reg. 2024/1689, 13 Jun 2024) verified via
browser_open (recitals 1-12: harmonised AI rules, high-risk common rules,
complementarity with data protection) — cited only for what was read.

